{
  "scenario": "APT29 and the SolarWinds Compromise (C0024) attributed to it, as ATT&CK Enterprise 20.1 records them: the SUNSPOT, SUNBURST, TEARDROP and Raindrop malware and the AdFind and Mimikatz tools, the techniques they use, from Compromise Software Supply Chain to forged SAML tokens and DCSync, with their parent techniques and tactics. Mitigations of those techniques, and the detection strategies for four of them with their Windows analytics and the data components they read, complete the picture. Every object, identifier and link is taken from the ATT&CK 20.1 Enterprise bundle.",
